DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261211
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261212
SUMMARY:Deadline: Golden Fleece Award 2027 (Ireland\, two EUR 10\,000 award
 s)
DESCRIPTION:Annual award from the Lillias Mitchell Trust recognising craft 
 and visual artists connected to Ireland. AWARDS: EUR 10\,000 each to two w
 inners\, one in Visual Art and one in Craft + Applied Art (total fund usua
 lly around EUR 30\,000)\; shortlisted artists also receive a smaller finan
 cial award\, amount to be confirmed.\n\nOrganisation: The Golden Fleece Aw
 ard (Lillias Mitchell Trust)\nLocation: Island of Ireland (artists living 
 and working in Ireland or Northern Ireland)\, plus Irish-born artists work
 ing overseas.\nAward: EUR 10\,000 each for two category winners (Visual Ar
 t\, and Craft + Applied Art)\; total fund usually around EUR 30\,000\, wit
 h shortlisted artists also receiving a smaller financial award (amount to 
 be confirmed). No application fee.\nDuration: Annual award for ongoing pra
 ctice\; apply online.\n\nMore: https://www.goldenfleeceaward.com/how-to-ap
 ply/guidelines?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.goldenfleeceaward.com/how-to-apply/guidelines?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Island of Ireland (artists living and working in Ireland or Northe
 rn Ireland)\, plus Irish-born artists working overseas.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:costar-southbank-creative-intelligence-award-2027@artificialnouveau.git
 hub.io
DTSTAMP:20261111T003228Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART:20261217T133000Z
DTEND:20261217T140000Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 14:00 GMT: The Creative Intelligence Award 2027 (CoSTAR Na
 tional Lab x Southbank Centre)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 17 Dec 2026 at 14:00 GMT.\n\nA new co-commission from Co
 STAR National Lab and Southbank Centre to take a creative technology idea 
 that is ready to be completed\, honed or technically advanced through focu
 sed R&D\, then present it to audiences at Southbank Centre's Creative Inte
 lligence festival in autumn 2027.\n\nOrganisation: CoSTAR National Lab and
  Southbank Centre\, supported by UKRI\nLocation: UK (lead applicant must b
 e a UK-registered company\; project activity UK-based). Prototyping at Pin
 ewood Studios\; showcase at Southbank Centre\, London.\nAward: GBP 50\,000
  grant (one award)\, plus up to GBP 25\,000 in AI compute and cloud credit
 s\, 2 x 5 days studio access at Pinewood Studios\, a six-week CoSTAR proto
 typing team sprint\, 3 days pre-show testing\, Southbank curatorial and pr
 oducing support\, and 20 hours of mentorship. No application fee.\nDuratio
 n: R&D development through 2027\, presented at Creative Intelligence festi
 val\, Southbank Centre\, autumn 2027\n\nMore: https://www.costarnetwork.co
 .uk/calls/the-creative-intelligence-award?utm_source=artificialnouveaugran
 tdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.costarnetwork.co.uk/calls/the-creative-intelligence-award?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:UK (lead applicant must be a UK-registered company\; project activ
 ity UK-based). Prototyping at Pinewood Studios\; showcase at Southbank Cen
 tre\, London.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:royal-institute-philosophy-essay-prize-2026-humans-and-ai@artificialnou
 veau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261111T003228Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART:20261231T232900Z
DTEND:20261231T235900Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 GMT: Royal Institute of Philosophy Essay Prize 2026:
  Humans and AI
DESCRIPTION:Closes 31 Dec 2026 at 23:59 GMT.\n\nThe Royal Institute of Phil
 osophy's annual essay prize asks for an original philosophical essay on th
 e 2026 topic\, Humans and AI. Essays of up to 8\,000 words\, anonymised fo
 r review\, are submitted by email. No eligibility restrictions are stated.
  Note: the Cambridge Core prize page still shows the older 2024 call at a 
 different amount\; the institute's own announcement is current.\n\nOrganis
 ation: Royal Institute of Philosophy\nLocation: Remote submission by email
 . Open internationally.\nAward: GBP 1\,000 cash plus GBP 500 of Cambridge 
 University Press books\; the winning essay is published in the journal Phi
 losophy.\nDuration: One-off essay prize.\n\nMore: https://royalinstituteph
 ilosophy.org/news/humans-and-ai-our-2026-philosophy-essay-prize-topic/?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://royalinstitutephilosophy.org/news/humans-and-ai-our-2026-philos
 ophy-essay-prize-topic/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
LOCATION:Remote submission by email. Open internationally.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
